# TypeScript Types & Interfaces Skill

## Purpose
Types are shared across all apps via `@tbe/types` (DB + API types) and `@tbe/interface` (component + page props). This skill prevents duplication, ensures separation between database types and UI types, and enforces the naming conventions established in the codebase.

## Rules
1. **DB model interfaces go in `packages/types/src/database.ts`** — types like `UserModel`, `CourseModel`.
2. **API request/response types go in `packages/types/src/api.ts`** — types like `APIResponseType`, `APIMakeRequestProps`.
3. **Component props interfaces go in `packages/interface/src/Components.ts`** — types consumed by `@tbe/components`.
4. **Page-level props go in `packages/interface/src/page.ts`** — `PageProps`, `GetSEOMetaResponseType`.
5. **Never use `type` for object shapes that extend or are extended** — use `interface`. Use `type` for unions and intersections.
6. **Never use `any`** — use `unknown` for truly unknown values. If you must, add a `// eslint-disable-next-line @typescript-eslint/no-explicit-any` comment with a reason.
7. **Always export named exports** — no default exports from type files.
8. **Enum-style string unions go in `packages/types/src/database.ts`** — e.g., `UserRoleType`, `GoalType`. Never use TypeScript `enum` keyword — use `type` unions.
9. **All `APIResponseType` shapes must have `status: boolean`** — this is the universal contract.
10. **Use `as const` for constant object maps** — not TypeScript enums.
11. **Prefix interfaces with nothing** — no `I` prefix (no `IUser`). Use `UserModel`, `UserProps`, etc.

## Patterns

### Database type (in packages/types/src/database.ts)
```ts
// Union type for DB enums
export type SubscriptionType = "FREE" | "PREMIUM" | "ENTERPRISE";

// Model interface mirroring Mongoose schema
export interface UserModel {
  _id: string;
  email: string;
  name: string;
  role: UserRoleType;
  isOnboarded: boolean;
  subscription: SubscriptionType;
  createdAt: Date;
  updatedAt: Date;
}
```

### API response type (in packages/types/src/api.ts)
```ts
export interface GetUserResponseType {
  status: boolean;
  data?: UserModel;
  message?: string;
  error?: string;
}
```

### Component props interface (in packages/interface/src/Components.ts)
```ts
export interface ResourceCardProps {
  /** Title displayed in the card header */
  title: string;
  /** Optional description text */
  description?: string;
  /** Loading skeleton state */
  isLoading?: boolean;
  /** Visual variant */
  variant?: "DEFAULT" | "COMPACT" | "FEATURED";
  /** Callback when card is clicked */
  onClick?: () => void;
}
```

### Constant map with as const
```ts
// packages/types/src/database.ts or packages/constants/src/
export const SUBSCRIPTION_TIERS = {
  FREE: "FREE",
  PREMIUM: "PREMIUM",
  ENTERPRISE: "ENTERPRISE",
} as const;

export type SubscriptionType = (typeof SUBSCRIPTION_TIERS)[keyof typeof SUBSCRIPTION_TIERS];
```

## Anti-Patterns

### ❌ TypeScript enum keyword
```ts
// BAD — TypeScript enums have runtime overhead and don't work with const assertions
enum UserRole { TECH_STUDENT = "TECH_STUDENT", WORKING_PROFESSIONAL = "WORKING_PROFESSIONAL" }
```
```ts
// GOOD
export type UserRoleType = "TECH_STUDENT" | "WORKING_PROFESSIONAL" | "NON_TECH_STUDENT";
```

### ❌ Using any without justification
```ts
// BAD
const processData = (data: any) => { return data.value; };
```
```ts
// GOOD
const processData = (data: unknown) => {
  if (typeof data === "object" && data !== null && "value" in data) {
    return (data as { value: string }).value;
  }
  return null;
};
```

### ❌ Duplicating types across packages
```ts
// BAD — UserModel defined in both apps/api AND packages/types
// apps/api/src/lib/interfaces/database.ts
interface UserModel { email: string; /* ... */ }
// packages/types/src/database.ts
interface UserModel { email: string; /* ... */ }  // duplicate!
```
```ts
// GOOD — single source in packages/types, import everywhere else
import type { UserModel } from "@tbe/types";
```

### ❌ I-prefixed interface names
```ts
// BAD
interface IButtonProps { text: string; }
interface IUserModel { email: string; }
```
```ts
// GOOD
interface ButtonProps { text: string; }
interface UserModel { email: string; }
```
